---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CssFormatter from '../../components/CssFormatter.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="CSS Formatter" description="Indent and format minified or single-line CSS into readable, rule-per-line syntax.">
  <CssFormatter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why formatting helps beyond aesthetics</h2>
  <p>Minified CSS pulled from a browser's dev tools or a build output is nearly impossible to scan for a specific rule — formatting it back into one property per line makes it possible to actually read and debug.</p>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your minified or single-line CSS.</li>
    <li>The formatted version appears instantly with proper indentation and line breaks.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>Input: <code>{`.btn{color:#fff;background:#10b981;padding:8px 16px}`}</code></p>
  <p>Output:</p>
  <pre><code>{`.btn {
  color: #fff;
  background: #10b981;
  padding: 8px 16px;
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming this validates CSS syntax.</strong> It only reformats spacing and structure — invalid property names or values pass through unchanged.</li>
    <li><strong>Losing track of specificity when reformatting a large stylesheet</strong> — formatting doesn't reorganize cascade order, so review carefully when working with legacy CSS.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Making a minified production CSS file readable for debugging</li>
    <li>Cleaning up CSS pasted from a design tool export</li>
    <li>Reviewing a third-party stylesheet before integrating it</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does this support SCSS/LESS syntax?</strong> This handles plain CSS — preprocessor-specific syntax (nesting, variables, mixins) isn't specially parsed.</p>
</ToolLayout>
